{
  "enabled": true,
  "name": "Code Quality Analyzer",
  "description": "Monitors source code file changes and provides suggestions for code quality improvements including code smells, design patterns, best practices, readability, maintainability, and performance optimizations",
  "version": "1",
  "when": {
    "type": "fileEdited",
    "patterns": [
      "**/*.py",
      "**/*.js",
      "**/*.ts",
      "**/*.java",
      "**/*.cpp",
      "**/*.c",
      "**/*.go",
      "**/*.rs",
      "**/*.rb",
      "**/*.php"
    ]
  },
  "then": {
    "type": "askAgent",
    "prompt": "A source code file has been modified. Please analyze the changes in the file for potential improvements:\n\n1. **Code Smells**: Identify any code smells such as:\n   - Long methods or functions\n   - Duplicate code\n   - Large classes\n   - Too many parameters\n   - Dead code\n   - Magic numbers or strings\n\n2. **Design Patterns**: Suggest applicable design patterns that could improve the code structure\n\n3. **Best Practices**: Check for:\n   - Proper error handling\n   - Input validation\n   - Security concerns\n   - Resource management\n   - Naming conventions\n   - Code organization\n\n4. **Readability**: Evaluate:\n   - Code clarity and simplicity\n   - Comment quality and necessity\n   - Variable and function naming\n   - Code formatting consistency\n\n5. **Maintainability**: Assess:\n   - Code modularity\n   - Separation of concerns\n   - Testability\n   - Documentation completeness\n\n6. **Performance**: Look for:\n   - Inefficient algorithms\n   - Unnecessary computations\n   - Memory leaks\n   - Database query optimization opportunities\n   - Caching opportunities\n\nPlease provide specific, actionable suggestions while maintaining the existing functionality. Focus on improvements that will have the most impact on code quality."
  }
}